-Phase 3: We check the IP 18.223.186.129 that is not being moving laterally to other machines. We don't find any connection between the clients and the malicious IP. We check that the 
infected computer hasn't made any connection to other IP's in the network too as it's vulnerable now.


-Phase 4: The malware creates a user called HelpDesk in the victim's machine. It moves the account to Administrator's group and to the Remote Desktop Users group too. 


-Phase 5: We check the timestamps of the actions and we can see that the interval of time has been in a short period of time which it can lead to the option that it was a spearphishing where
